meta {
  name: CreateIgnoresInternalFields
  type: http
  seq: 6
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/web/bon/{{bonnr}}/lijn
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
  Accept: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "artnr": "TESTART-INTERNAL",
    "omschrijving": "Test regel - internal fields must be ignored",
    "aantal": 1,
    "vprijs": 10.0,
    "offnr": 12345,
    "versie": 1,
    "olijnnr": 7,
    "swLed": true,
    "swSikta": true,
    "montage": true,
    "ledmontage": true,
    "circuit": 99,
    "recupel": 1.5,
    "meer_min": 2.5,
    "off_aantal": 4,
    "swStdPrijs": true,
    "uitverkoop": true,
    "SiktaKleurKodes": "ABC",
    "gereserv": 999
  }
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 201
  res.body.bonnr: eq {{bonnr}}
}

script:post-response {
  bru.setVar("internalFieldsLijnnr", res.body.lijnnr);
}

docs {
  Iteratie D - Onderdeel 2 regression proof: this request hits the
  PUBLIC POST /web/bon/{bonnr}/lijn contract (Luna.BusinessLogic.
  BonLijnBE:CreateBonLijn, which delegates to CreateBonLijnInternal with
  piExplicitLijnnr = 0) and includes every field that is ONLY meant to be
  settable via the internal offerte-conversion path (offnr, versie,
  olijnnr, swLed, swSikta, montage, ledmontage, circuit, recupel,
  meer_min, off_aantal, swStdPrijs, uitverkoop, SiktaKleurKodes,
  gereserv). None of these fields are part of ttBonLijn's response
  shape, so the response body itself can't prove they were ignored -
  the response only proves the request still succeeds and behaves like
  a normal item-line create (i.e. the extra keys don't break anything).
  backend-tester should additionally spot-check the DB row for
  {{bonnr}}/{{internalFieldsLijnnr}} (bonlijn.offnr/versie/olijnnr/
  swLed/circuit/recupel/gereserv etc.) and confirm they are all still
  0/""/no - this was verified manually during implementation (see
  handoff note) but isn't asserted here since the API has no field to
  read them back through.
}
